    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The parts supply the whole route: the two conditions (k>0 and Δ<0), then Δ, then the inequality, then the combination. The student computes Δ=4-4k² with a=c=k, factorises and solves 4-4k²<0 with no graph supplied, so must picture the downward parabola in k to get the outside region. They then intersect k<-1 or k>1 with k>0. The only change of representation is moving between conditions on the parabola and inequalities in k, which is routine and linked. This is harder than the single-idea explanation in p68-q11 and a little easier than p67-q8, which asks for open-ended interpretation of two representations.",
